  "release_changes": [
    "Explicit user-supplied model/data/output paths replace development-machine defaults; cluster launchers and embedded credentials are not selected.",
    "SFT conversion rejects malformed tool pairing and media, retains complete text observations, and never inserts fake tool responses or converts missing rewards to zero.",
    "Full-conversation causal-LM loss is retained; only batch padding is masked. Overlength examples fail instead of being truncated.",
    "Qwen3-VL uses its matching Transformers model class and AutoProcessor; a causal-LM path is available. Single-process LoRA training uses a separately pinned optional stack.",
    "Merging requires an explicit base model and saves the processor/tokenizer. Existing output is protected.",
    "GRPO/GDPO-style preprocessing is independent of Slime; groups and validity masks are explicit, dictionary reward keys are unambiguous, and missing dimensions reject a group instead of falling back to an aggregate.",
    "Task selection is explicit and manifest paths are relative by default. No benchmark train/test split or hidden exclusions are inferred.",
    "Local regression tests cover data integrity, reward semantics, actual tiny-model CPU LoRA updates and merge-logit equivalence for both model-loading paths."
  ],
  "not_included": [
    "Model weights and training data",
    "Historical cluster launchers and logs",
    "Slime/Megatron source and full RL rollout/training integration",
    "Process-reward and rubric-calibration pipelines",
    "GPU-scale reproduction configurations"
  ],
  "validation_scope": "The complete development workflow was tested locally. Release checks cover the selected components, not a repeat of all historical GPU experiments."
}
